cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyundoom (동현둠): a browser laboratory for the shareware DOOM Episode 1, with the stage, skill, health, armour and the IDDQD and IDKFA cheats set through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab8"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab8/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyundoom is a browser-based, noncommercial hobby project that runs the
  nine maps of the shareware DOOM Episode 1, Knee-Deep in the Dead, through a
  modified build of Cloudflare's doom-wasm port of Chocolate Doom. The starting
  map (1-9), skill (1-5), health (1-200), armour (0-200) and the IDDQD and
  IDKFA cheats (0 or 1) are chosen by six integers printed by a program written
  in the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang; cheats typed during play
  are disabled. All six shareware weapons are given at the start of every map,
  and play uses the keyboard only. The repository is distributed under the GNU
  GPL 2.0 together with the modified engine source; the unmodified shareware
  DOOM1.WAD (v1.9) is (c) id Software and is not covered by the GPL. DOOM is a
  trademark of id Software; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  id Software, ZeniMax, Bethesda, Microsoft or Cloudflare. See CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - DOOM
  - shareware
  - WebAssembly
  - Chocolate Doom
  - esoteric programming language
